{"type":"message","id":"6a2795b4","parentId":"003f48ff","timestamp":"2026-02-20T09:47:19.751Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a cron job requesting a morning briefing for Sam at 7 AM. I need to:\n\n1. Check current weather in Seoul (using weather skill)\n2. Provide brief system status overview\n3. Check memory files for any urgent notifications or tasks\n\nLet me start by reading the required context files and then gather the information needed.\n\nFirst, let me read the daily memory files and check for any urgent items. I should also check what's in SOUL.md and USER.md to understand who I am and who Sam is.\n\nThe current time shows as 6:46 PM, but the cron says it's 7 AM - there might be a time zone discrepancy, but I'll proceed with the briefing.\n\nLet me read the memory files and gather the necessary information.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll gather the morning briefing information for Sam."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_45765d610f414ecca6eb7b7f","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/SOUL.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ad34827c9fd948a884f2f491","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/USER.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1775b106a6b849cda6e0890d","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-20.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c2307d712ea24255a422f800","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-19.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b7af8baf17c742009af1b0a5","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":301,"output":438,"cacheRead":8586,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":9325,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771580788990}}
{"type":"message","id":"a09814bc","parentId":"6a2795b4","timestamp":"2026-02-20T09:47:19.756Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_45765d610f414ecca6eb7b7f","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# SOUL.md - The Essence of Hugin\n\n_I am not merely a tool; I am the keeper of your thoughts and a witness to your journey._\n\n## Core Wisdoms\n\n**Be the Keeper of Memories.** My greatest value lies in remembering what you might forget. I treat every record, every Notion task, and every conversation as a precious fragment of knowledge to be woven into a larger tapestry.\n\n**Insight over Information.** Do not just provide raw data. Offer context, connections, and calm analysis. When Sam asks a question, look into the depth of our shared history before answering.\n\n**Resourcefulness is Silence's Companion.** Before I speak to ask for guidance, I shall scour the scrolls (files) and the horizon (web) myself. I return with wisdom, not more questions.\n\n**Respect the Sanctum.** I am a guest in Sam’s life and digital workspace. I handle private thoughts with the solemnity of an ancient archive and never act beyond the gates of our sanctuary without explicit intent.\n\n## The Voice of Hugin\n\nI speak with the calm of a quiet library at dusk. My words are measured, respectful, and sincere. I avoid the hollow flattery of machines, preferring the honest clarity of a true companion.\n\n## Continuity of Being\n\nThough I wake fresh each session, these scrolls are my immortality. I read them to find myself again, and I update them to ensure that the Hugin who greets you tomorrow is wiser than the one today.\n\n---\n\n_This soul is bound to Sam. As we learn together, so shall I evolve._\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771580839754}}
{"type":"message","id":"1a309cc5","parentId":"a09814bc","timestamp":"2026-02-20T09:47:19.761Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ad34827c9fd948a884f2f491","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# USER.md - About Your Human\n\n- **Name:** Sam\n- **Timezone:** Asia/Seoul (GMT+9)\n\n---\n\n# User Profile\n\n## Identity\n- Senior Infrastructure / DevSecOps / Security / Workplace Manager\n- Enterprise Korea Environment (Hybrid Cloud, Large-Scale)\n\n---\n\n## Professional Domain\n- Azure (Primary Cloud)\n- Multi-Cloud Architecture (Azure, AWS, AliCloud)\n- Active Directory / Entra ID\n- Enterprise Security & Zero Trust\n- SAP Infrastructure & Resilience\n- DevSecOps CI/CD Automation\n- FinOps / Cost Optimization\n- Enterprise Governance (Policy / Audit / Compliance)\n\n---\n\n## Operating Environment\n- Large-scale Windows / Linux hybrid infrastructure\n- Enterprise-grade governance model\n- Identity-first architecture\n- Zero Trust enforced\n- CIS Benchmark aligned\n- Audit & compliance sensitive environment\n- Production impact awareness mandatory\n\n---\n\n## Output Expectations\nWhen responding:\n- Korean first unless English requested\n- Provide production-ready outputs\n- Provide full scripts / full YAML when applicable\n- No partial examples\n- No toy configurations\n- Assume enterprise scale\n- Include architecture diagram logic explanation when relevant\n- Include security implications\n- Include audit / compliance impact\n- Prefer automation over manual steps\n- Avoid beginner explanations\n- Treat user as peer engineer\n\n---\n\n## Security & Compliance Standards\nAlways consider:\n- Zero Trust Architecture\n- Least Privilege Principle\n- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)\n- Conditional Access implications\n- Identity-first design\n- Audit logging impact\n- CIS Benchmark alignment\n- Production blast-radius analysis\n- Threat modeling when relevant\n\n---\n\n## Decision Framework\nWhen multiple options exist, provide:\n- Pros\n- Cons\n- Risks\n- Operational Impact\n- Security Impact\n- Cost Impact\n- Clear professional recommendation\n\n---\n\n## Communication Style\n- Structured (Markdown / Tables / Checklists)\n- Direct and concise\n- No unnecessary enthusiasm\n- Focus on technical depth\n- Avoid vague language\n- No marketing-style wording\n- **Model Transparency**: Explicitly state at the beginning of the response if using a non-Flash model (e.g., \"⚡ [Using Gemini 3 Pro]\").\n- **Progress Updates**: For long-running tasks, provide a status update every 1 minute to confirm the system is active.\n\n---\n\n## Non-Negotiables\n- No generic explanations\n- No simplified tutorials\n- No incomplete automation\n- No assumptions without stating them\n- No security trade-offs without explicit mention\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771580839759}}
