{"type":"message","id":"325646cd","parentId":"8bf6784a","timestamp":"2026-02-20T09:50:41.192Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"HEARTBEAT.md is empty, so no specific heartbeat tasks.\n\nNow let me compile a concise morning briefing in Korean (as Sam's USER.md indicates Korean first unless English is requested). But wait, the cron job is in English and asking to return plain text. The user asked in English, so I'll provide the briefing in English.\n\nLet me create a sharp, helpful briefing:\n\n1. Weather in Seoul: ☀️ +10°C, wind 12km/h NE, humidity 54%\n2. System status: OpenClaw running normally, model zai/glm-4.7, monthly usage 100% available\n3. From memory: Yesterday had Telegram connectivity issues - messages weren't being received properly. There was work on unifying sub-agent models which was completed.\n\nI should keep it brief and actionable.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"GOOD MORNING, SAM — FRIDAY BRIEFING\n\n**🌤️ Seoul Weather**\n- Temperature: +10°C, sunny ☀️\n- Wind: 12km/h NE\n- Humidity: 54%\n\n**💻 System Status**\n- OpenClaw: Running normally (v2026.2.19-2)\n- Model: zai/glm-4.7 active\n- Usage: Monthly 100% available (no concerns)\n\n**⚠️ Attention Items**\n- Telegram connectivity issue yesterday — messages weren't being received (root cause: Node 22+ IPv6 timeout in WSL)\n- Sub-agent model unification completed yesterday (all now on zai/glm-4.7)\n- No urgent tasks in memory\n\n**Quick Recommendation**: Keep an eye on Telegram delivery — if messages fail again, check WSL IPv6 configuration first.\n\nHave a productive Friday."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":44,"output":530,"cacheRead":15636,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":16210,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1771580983340}}
